>> title: Lengua
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, tongue, mexican, simmer, tacos
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: lengua, beef tongue, taco de lengua, tacos de lengua, lengua en su jugo, cow tongue
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-verde
>> servings: 8
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the skin comes off a hot tongue in one piece and off a cooled one in shreds, and reheating does not get it back
>> step.1: simmer 3 hr
>> step.2: peel hot, trim the root
>> step.3: dice 1/2-in
>> step.4: crisp on the comal 6 min

Simmer @beef tongue{3%lb}(1.4 kg; whole), @white onion{1}(halved), @garlic{1%head}(halved across), @bay leaves{2}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, and @kosher salt{2%Tbs} in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) in a #stockpot{} for ~simmer{3%hr}, barely bubbling, until a knife slides into the thick end with no resistance.

Peel @&(~1)cooked tongue{} while it is still too hot to hold comfortably — the skin comes away in sheets, and it will not come away at all once it cools — and trim the gristle and fat from the root end.

Dice @&(~1)peeled tongue{} into 1/2-in cubes.

Crisp @&(~1)diced tongue{} on a hot #comal{} in @lard{2%Tbs} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} for ~sear{6%min}, until the cut faces brown and the middle stays soft as pot roast.
